    "required_age": 0,
    "is_free": false,
    "detailed_description": "<span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2843540/extras/02daeba60c8f190f893dcbce9f991280.avif?t=1714788060\" width=600 height=81 /></span><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2843540/extras/2d713344c74c7ab43cb8e108e9101485.avif?t=1714788060\" width=600 height=80 /></span><br><br>Aldercourt City Council, in association with Sequre Transport Authority, welcome you into Aldercourt Station.<br><br>Aldercourt Station is a sprawling and expansive addition to London's Travel Network. Come get lost amonst its tile halls and take in the scenery as you pass through its liminal spaces.<br><br>It can be a little difficult to find your way through the station however - Follow the signs, keep your eyes open and you'll be just fine.<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2843540/extras/94d937ff3d1a6261694a87cda6f659c6.avif?t=1714788060\" width=600 height=91 /></span><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >What is Midnight Monitor: Aldercourt?</h2><br>Midnight Monitor: Aldercourt is a &quot;walking simulator&quot; anomaly spotting game, heavily inspired by creepy internet stories around the Backrooms, the concept of Liminal Spaces, and other games of this genre such as &quot;The Exit 8&quot;.<br><br>In Midnight Monitor: Aldercourt, you will need to watch your surroundings for any changes (big or small) as you loop through the Station. Anything can change - Walls and windows can appear, gravity can change, people can act strangely... And your life could be in danger.<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2843540/extras/a6a763b91af358b39252611b7b51f2df.avif?t=1714788060\" width=600 height=176 /></span><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Play Time</h2>The game features 40+ anomalies for players to find with an approx. playtime of 15 Mins - 2 Hours. Completionists may opt to find every anomaly.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Is Midnight Monitor: Aldercourt scary?</h2>There are some mild jumpscares depending on how sensitive you are to sudden changes.<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2843540/extras/891b844b05e12bf763d2b603536e5c4a.poster.avif?t=1714788060\" width=600 height=336 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2843540/extras/891b844b05e12bf763d2b603536e5c4a.webm?t=1714788060\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2843540/extras/891b844b05e12bf763d2b603536e5c4a.mp4?t=1714788060\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Is Midnight Monitor: Aldercourt a complete game?</h2>Midnight Monitor: Aldercourt is a complete game. Some additional anomalies may be added in the future, but it is releasing feature-complete.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >How does Midnight Monitor: Aldercourt tie into the Midnight Monitor series?</h2>The security firm &quot;Sequre&quot; featured through Midnight Monitor: Anomaly Watch features again in this game with some small callbacks to &quot;Anomaly Watch&quot;. The plan is to continue growing the Midnight Monitor ethos as the series grows.<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2843540/extras/0dac76292d5df113d1490a1619fdf25f.avif?t=1714788060\" width=600 height=226 /></span>",
